ng ${a}_{22}$, ${a}_{41}$, and ${a}_{42}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form." "The minimum set is $a_{41}$ and $a_{42}$. Replace these 2 entries with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 1, 2, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. \n\nRestoring $a_{41}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 1, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. Restoring $a_{42}$ would put the leading entry of row 4 in column 2, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 3. No set with fewer than 2 replacements satisfies both the leading-entry order and zero-row conditions.\n\nEntries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero."] [:db/ensure 17592186619081 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186619098 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186409324 :performance/assessment-accuracy 0.9538885174664806 0.9958315574664807] [:db/ensure 17592186409324 :performance/validate] [:db/cas 17592186524200 :progress/assessment-accuracy 0.6894191008102029 0.8] [:db/cas 17592186524200 :progress/assessment-mass 0.6666666666666666 0.0] [:db/ensure 17592186524200 :progress/validate] [:db/cas 17592186524201 :progress/assessment-accuracy 0.7155417527999327 0.8] [:db/cas 17592186524201 :progress/assessment-mass 0.5 0.0] [:db/ensure 17592186524201 :progress/validate] [:db/cas 17592186524202 :progress/assessment-accuracy 0.7155417527999327 0.8] [:db/cas 17592186524